{{!--
  VCarve Pro post — wood routing on Mach3-class controllers (Laguna Swift, etc.)

  Tuned for the **VCarve Pro environment** in WorkTrack3D:
  - Wood-routing-friendly spindle warmup (G4 dwell after M3)
  - Conservative safe Z (uses machine.workAreaMm.z)
  - Mach3-style program tape markers (% on first/last lines)
  - Dust-collection M-codes gated on the `dustCollection` PostContext flag
    (roadmap [ID-0004]). When the flag is set, M7 is emitted after the
    spindle warm-up dwell and M9 is emitted before the spindle-off ramp.
    When the flag is unset, the lines stay commented out so a bench setup
    that hasn't wired M7/M9 isn't surprised.
  - Spindle cool-down ramp: M5 followed by G4 P3 (3 s dwell) so the VFD
    decelerates before the safe-Z retract — keeps bit in-chuck from
    flinging loose when a coasting spindle hits a part edge.
  - No peck cycles by default; drill ops emit explicit Z moves
  - Single-tool program by default — extend if you wire ATC into your Laguna

  Controller-dialect note (roadmap [ID-0063]):
  The Laguna Swift 5×10's RichAuto A-series handheld accepts Mach3-compatible
  G-code as a strict superset: G21/G90/G17, G0/G1/G2/G3, M3/M5, S/F, M7/M9,
  M30, and `%` tape markers are all honored. This post therefore uses the
  existing `dialect: "mach3"` enum rather than introducing a new `richauto_a`
  enum (avoids a schema migration per CLAUDE.md Safety Rule 2 for zero
  behavioural gain). When a future post needs RichAuto-only syntax that
  Mach3 rejects, open a separate template rather than diverging this one.

  Lines starting with ";" are operator-visible comments in the output file.
  Template context keys: resources/posts/README.md (PostContext / renderPost).
--}}
%
; VCarve Pro post — {{machine.name}} ({{machine.id}})
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; UNVERIFIED G-CODE — verify every line against your Mach3/Mach4 setup before
; running on the machine. Output is not guaranteed safe for any real machine.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Wood routing checklist:
; [1] Material clamped flat to spoilboard, no warps under bit path
; [2] Tool-length set: V-bit at sharp tip, end mill at flute bottom, drill at tip
; [3] WCS X0/Y0 at workpiece corner per VCarve Pro setup; Z0 = top of stock
; [4] Dust collection ON (set `dustCollection: true` to emit M7/M9, or
;     uncomment manually if your controller wires different M-codes)
; [5] Air-cut first: spindle off, Z high, 25–50% feed override
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Work area (mm): {{machine.workAreaMm.x}} x {{machine.workAreaMm.y}} x {{machine.workAreaMm.z}}
{{#if machine.maxSpindleRpm}}; Spindle max: {{machine.maxSpindleRpm}} RPM
{{/if}}{{#if operationLabel}}; Operation: {{operationLabel}}
{{/if}}; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{{units}}        ; G21=mm / G20=inch — must match controller defaults at power-on
G90              ; absolute distance mode
G17              ; XY plane (typical for G2/G3 arcs)
G94              ; feed in units/min
{{#if wcsLine}}; Active work offset — verify fixture zero matches G54–G59 selection
{{wcsLine}}
{{/if}}; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Spindle on (dialect snippet — Mach3 emits M3 S<rpm>)
{{spindleOn}}
G4 P2.0          ; dwell 2 s for spindle to reach commanded RPM (wood router warmup)
{{#if dustCollection}}M7               ; dust collection ON (VCarve Pro dustCollection flag)
{{else}}; M7              ; coolant/mist OFF — set dustCollection flag to emit M7 here
{{/if}}; M8              ; flood coolant — typically OFF for wood; uncomment for wet ops
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; [ID-0110] Pre-cut safe-Z lift -- mirrors carvera_3axis.hbs / carvera_4axis.hbs
; so the first XY/Z move below executes from a known clearance regardless of
; what Z the controller booted into or where the previous job left it.
G0 Z{{machine.workAreaMm.z}} ; safe Z retract before toolpath -- uses machine work area Z height
{{#each toolpathLines}}
{{this}}
{{/each}}
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{{#if dustCollection}}M9               ; dust collection OFF (VCarve Pro dustCollection flag)
{{else}}; M9              ; coolant/dust OFF — set dustCollection flag to emit M9 here
{{/if}}; Spindle off (dialect snippet — usually M5)
{{spindleOff}}
G4 P3.0          ; dwell 3 s — spindle cool-down ramp before safe-Z retract
G0 Z{{machine.workAreaMm.z}} ; safe Z retract — uses machine work area Z height
G0 X0 Y0                     ; park X Y at WCS origin (adjust to your preferred home)
M30              ; program end + rewind (Mach3 expects M30, not M2)
%
